& [CanonicalRecord: FinalSlicingSurface] is the processed planning authority for dependency-isolated final slicing
  + [canonical_uuid] is 8fcaf245-fda7-4fc3-aeab-e5847cd44068
  + [source_manifest_uuid] is f2a457c8-f50d-4ae7-8e9b-54fad1f5d231
  + [exploded_uuid] is fe248262-e0fd-4045-b23a-f99eddf6ada5
  + [surface_uuid] is 38266ad5-abd9-4907-bb66-aab981064d7d
  + [authority_scope] is dependency closure, chunk isolation, final-slice readiness, activation gates, and model routing
  + [implementation_scope] is planning and slice-preparation authority only
  + [depends_on] is docs/canonical/LangSOP_Whole_Pie_Working_Pattern.canonical.sop

  = must: use docs/planning/Final_Slicing_Surface.v1.sop as the current final-slicing surface
  = must: classify dependencies before minting final slices
  = must: allow only accepted_boundary_input dependencies outside a final-slice-ready chunk
  = must: gate chunks whose needed upstream outputs are not yet accepted
  = must: pull shared proof and fixture work into the local chunk it proves
  - never: mint final slices from a chunk with forbidden_external_dependency

& [CanonicalDependencyClosureContract] is the dependency isolation rule
  + [internal_dependency] is a dependency resolved inside the chunk boundary
  + [accepted_boundary_input] is signed or proof-backed material imported as stable input
  + [activation_gate] is an upstream output required before the chunk may be final-sliced
  + [forbidden_external_dependency] is unresolved work outside the chunk boundary

  = must: convert forbidden_external_dependency into internal_dependency or activation_gate before slicing
  = must: preserve activation_gate state visibly on manager surfaces
  = must: mark final slices stale when accepted_boundary_input changes or invalidates

& [CanonicalContiguousChunkContract] is the contract for final-slicing chunks
  + [chunk] is a contiguous product territory with shared local data, procedure, proof, or surface purpose
  + [chunk_seal_state_set] is accepted_boundary, final_slice_ready, gated, blocked, or superseded
  + [chunk_record] is final_slicing_chunk with included portions, local proof leg, boundary inputs, activation gates, internal dependency order, final slice families, model route, and verification route

  = must: keep P8 fixture and proof work split into local legs P8a through P8e
  = must: keep downstream chunks parked behind accepted upstream outputs
  = must: keep FSC1 as the only immediate final-slice-ready chunk

& [CanonicalFinalChunkSet] is the sealed chunk set
  + [FSC0] is accepted authority baseline
  + [FSC1] is foundation contracts
  + [FSC2] is planning coordination
  + [FSC3] is runtime graph proof
  + [FSC4] is surface projection
  + [FSC5] is operations safety envelope

  = must: treat FSC0 as accepted input, not new implementation work
  = must: final-slice FSC1 first
  = must: not final-slice FSC2 until FSC1 foundation contract pack is accepted
  = must: not final-slice FSC3 until FSC1 and FSC2 accepted outputs exist
  = must: not final-slice FSC4 until FSC1, FSC2, FSC3, and local projection fixtures are accepted
  = must: not final-slice FSC5 until FSC1 through FSC4 are accepted and a safety source is preserved

& [CanonicalFinalSliceRule] is the rule for the next operation after this surface
  + [next_allowed_operation] is mint FSC1 final slices
  + [required_slice_fields] is authority_basis, chunk_ref, boundary_input_set, internal_dependency_set, expected_output_set, verification_oracle, model_route, forbidden_scope, and completion_review_required
  + [first_model_route] is requires deeper reasoning

  = must: include completed-work review after each FSC1 slice
  = must: rebake FSC1 if a slice discovers a schema or operator boundary contradiction
  = should: route later fixture-generation slices to GPT-5.3-Codex-Spark after schema and operator contracts stabilize

